course: dictionary
lesson: 3591
title: Fidget
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To fidget means to keep moving your hands, feet or body in small, restless ways. You might do it when you are bored, nervous or simply cannot sit still. «Stop fidgeting and listen,» the teacher said at assembly, so the children were meant to keep still.
explain: A fidget is a person who fidgets a lot, and a fidget toy is a small toy you squeeze, spin or click in your hands. «Use a fidget spinner or small toy in class only if the teacher allows it, because toys can distract you and others.» Some children focus better with one, but only when the teacher says yes.
explain: Context gives you clues. «Nervousness can make the voice shake and the hands fidget or tremble.» Hands that fidget are moving restlessly because of nerves, not doing a job. Try swapping in "move about restlessly": the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: To fidget means to move your hands, feet or body in small, restless ways.
fact: A fidget is a person who fidgets a lot.
fact: A fidget toy is a small toy made to be squeezed, spun or clicked in your hands.
fact: «Jack spends his whole £10 on the fidget toy everyone has, and two days later nobody cares about fidget toys any more.» A short craze like that is called a fad.
fact: Fidgets, as a noun, means restless movements.
exercise: At assembly the teacher says, «Stop fidgeting.» What does fidgeting mean here? | Falling asleep | *Moving about restlessly in small ways | Singing loudly with the class | Sitting perfectly still and silent
exercise: «Nervousness can make the hands fidget or tremble.» Find and copy the word that means shake slightly. | fidget | *tremble | hands | nervousness
exercise: What is a fidget toy? | A toy you read aloud from | *A small toy you squeeze, spin or click in your hands | A large toy for the playground | A toy that needs batteries and a screen
test: What is a fad, according to the example about the fidget toy? | A type of fidget spinner | A long-lasting hobby | *A short craze that soon fades | A school rule
test: Why might a teacher not allow a fidget toy in class? | It helps everyone sit still | Fidget toys are always free | *It can distract you and others | It makes the class too quiet
exam: Which word is a noun that means restless movements? | fidgeted | fidgeting | *fidgets | fidget
